# Predictive Modeler report

## Task

Assign all applicable emotion labels per track using multilabel classification with six separate binary targets: amazed-suprised__target, happy-pleased__target, relaxing-calm__target, quiet-still__target, sad-lonely__target, and angry-aggresive__target. Optimize micro-averaged F1, subject to complete fitted model size <=50000 bytes. Use a random split with seed 42 and the explicitly listed predictor columns; no official split column is present.

## Outcome

Status: succeeded. Stop reason: budget_exhausted.

## Agent rationale

All 3 allowed trials were trained and evaluated, and all were feasible under the 50,000-byte model-size constraint. The scaled regularized linear model achieved the best measured mean cross-validation micro-F1 (0.6336213541), outperforming the depth-one extra-trees model (0.3954571941) and baseline (0.0); no remaining trial budget is available for further hypotheses.

